-dirichlet-series","matters_for":["thm-dirichlet-series-half-plane-convergence","thm-dirichlet-series-absolute-half-plane-holomorphy","thm-dirichlet-series-summatory-integral","thm-multiplicative-dirichlet-series-euler-product","thm-von-mangoldt-logarithmic-derivative-zeta","ex-dirichlet-series-abscissa-boundaries"]},{"convention":"The defining zeta Dirichlet series names zeta only for Re(s)>1; outside that half-plane, zeta denotes its meromorphic continuation rather than an ordinary sum.","fixed_by":"def-riemann-zeta-function","matters_for":["thm-riemann-zeta-continuation-to-the-right-half-plane","thm-dirichlet-eta-representation","thm-riemann-zeta-meromorphic-continuation","rem-dirichlet-series-continuation-and-regularized-sums","cex-the-eta-series-represents-the-continuation-where-the-dirichlet-series-diverges","fs-riemann-zeta-is-given-by-its-dirichlet-series-for-all-s-not-one"]},{"convention":"The theta normalization is theta(t)=sum over all integers n of exp(-pi n^2 t), for t>0.","fixed_by":"def-jacobi-theta-function","matters_for":["thm-jacobi-theta-transformation","thm-theta-mellin-representation-of-completed-zeta","thm-riemann-zeta-meromorphic-continuation","thm-completed-riemann-zeta-functional-equation"]},{"convention":"For a finite graph, c-restricted means c-sparse or c-dense internally; c-sparse is a maximum-degree condition, while weak sparsity between sets is an edge-density condition and directional sparsity is not symmetric by definition.","fixed_by":"def-c-sparse-and-c-restricted-vertex-set","matters_for":["def-generalized-nice-finite-family","lem-a-complete-or-weakly-sparse-blockade-can-be-thinned-to-equal-subblocks-with-directional-sparsity","lem-generalized-niceness-yields-four-reduction-outcomes","lem-cy-restricted-generalized-niceness-yields-three-outcomes","lem-iterated-restricted-sparsification-reaches-the-target-scale"]},{"convention":"Generalized niceness quantifies over every complement-family-free graph and every epsilon in (0,1/2), after choosing one fixed tuple of constants for the family.","fixed_by":"def-generalized-nice-finite-family","matters_for":["lem-generalized-niceness-yields-four-reduction-outcomes","lem-cy-restricted-generalized-niceness-yields-three-outcomes","lem-a-large-cy-restricted-subgraph-in-the-three-outcome-theorem-forces-a-smaller-scale-restricted-subgraph","lem-constant-scale-restricted-generalized-niceness-yields-an-x-scale-restricted-subgraph-a-polynomial-clique-or-stable-set-or-a-blockade"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-p-adic-completion-is-a-field","statement":"The p-adic completion has well-defined field operations, an extended nonarchimedean absolute value, inverses for nonzero elements, and is complete.","used_by":["lem-p-adic-balls-are-clopen","thm-p-adic-completion-agrees-with-the-fraction-field-of-zp","thm-p-adic-digit-expansion","cor-p-adic-simple-root-lifting","thm-p-adic-newton-criterion","ex-p-adic-geometric-series"]},{"id":"thm-dirichlet-series-multiplication-convolution","statement":"On every half-plane where both Dirichlet series converge absolutely, their product is the Dirichlet series of the Dirichlet convolution.","used_by":["thm-multiplicative-dirichlet-series-euler-product","thm-von-mangoldt-logarithmic-derivative-zeta","cor-mobius-dirichlet-series-reciprocal-zeta","cor-divisor-dirichlet-series-zeta-square","cor-euler-totient-dirichlet-series","ex-mobius-reciprocal-zeta-coefficients"]},{"id":"def-riemann-zeta-function","statement":"For Re(s)>1, zeta(s)=sum from n=1 to infinity of n^{-s}, with n^{-s}=exp(-s log n).","used_by":["lem-riemann-zeta-dirichlet-series-converges-locally-uniformly","thm-euler-product-for-riemann-zeta","thm-riemann-zeta-continuation-to-the-right-half-plane","thm-dirichlet-eta-representation","thm-theta-mellin-representation-of-completed-zeta","thm-riemann-xi-is-entire-of-order-one"]},{"id":"thm-riemann-zeta-meromorphic-continuation","statement":"Zeta extends meromorphically to C, is holomorphic off 1, and has at 1 its sole simple pole of residue 1.","used_by":["thm-completed-riemann-zeta-functional-equation","thm-riemann-xi-is-entire-of-order-one","thm-special-values-of-riemann-zeta-at-integers","ex-zeta-zero-equals-minus-one-half","fs-riemann-zeta-is-entire","rem-dirichlet-series-continuation-and-regularized-sums"]},{"id":"thm-completed-riemann-zeta-functional-equation","statement":"Lambda extends meromorphically with simple poles at 0 and 1 and satisfies Lambda(s)=Lambda(1-s).","used_by":["thm-riemann-zeta-functional-equation","thm-riemann-xi-is-entire-of-order-one","thm-hadamard-product-for-riemann-xi","ex-splitting-the-theta-mellin-integral-isolates-the-two-polar-terms"]},{"id":"def-generalized-nice-finite-family","statement":"A finite graph family is generalized nice when fixed constants force one of its four stated blockade, clique-or-stable-set, pure-blockade, or restricted-subgraph alternatives for every complement-family-free graph and epsilon in (0,1/2).","used_by":["lem-generalized-niceness-yields-four-reduction-outcomes"]},{"id":"lem-generalized-niceness-yields-four-reduction-outcomes","statement":"A generalized nice, leaf-reducible, wonderful family has fixed constants giving one of four stated clique/stable-set, restricted-subgraph, pure-blockade, or large pure-pair outcomes for every y-restricted complement-family-free graph.","used_by":["lem-cy-restricted-generalized-niceness-yields-three-outcomes"]},{"id":"lem-cy-restricted-generalized-niceness-yields-three-outcomes","statement":"Fixed c,c1,c2,c3,c4 give every cy-restricted complement-family-free graph one of a polynomial clique/stable set, a pure blockade, or a y^{c4}-restricted subgraph of size at least y^{c3}|G|.","used_by":["lem-a-large-cy-restricted-subgraph-in-the-three-outcome-theorem-forces-a-smaller-scale-restricted-subgraph","lem-constant-scale-restricted-generalized-niceness-yields-an-x-scale-restricted-subgraph-a-polynomial-clique-or-stable-set-or-a-blockade"]},{"id":"lem-a-complete-or-weakly-sparse-blockade-can-be-thinned-to-equal-subblocks-with-directional-sparsity","statement":"A length-ceiling(epsilon^{-1}) blockade whose pairs are complete or weakly epsilon^a-sparse has equal subblocks of size ceiling(epsilon ceiling(m)) retaining complete pairs and becoming mutually epsilon^{a-5}-sparse directionally.","used_by":["lem-a-complete-or-weakly-sparse-blockade-yields-a-complete-subblockade-or-an-anticonnected-thinning","lem-generalized-niceness-yields-four-reduction-outcomes","ex-thinning-a-four-block-weakly-sparse-blockade-to-directional-sparse-subblocks"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"cor-classical-mobius-inversion","used_for":"Möbius identities in reciprocal-zeta and totient series.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-gamma-function-has-no-zeros","used_for":"Division by Gamma in the zeta continuation and trivial-zero analysis.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-von-mangoldt-mobius-inversion-formula","used_for":"Declared arithmetic support for the von Mangoldt identity.","opened":true},{"id":"def-adic-completion-of-a-module","used_for":"The compatible-residue model of Z_p used in the Q_p comparison.","opened":true},{"id":"def-anticonnected-graph-and-anticonnected-component","used_for":"Anticonnected block thinnings.","opened":true},{"id":"def-blockade-length-and-width","used_for":"Blockade length, width, and support throughout batch 15.","opened":true},{"id":"def-c-sparse-and-c-restricted-vertex-set","used_for":"Restrictedness and maximum-degree sparsity conventions.","opened":true},{"id":"def-clique-stable-set-and-numbers","used_for":"Clique and stable-set alternatives.","opened":true},{"id":"def-completely-multiplicative-arithmetic-function","used_for":"Geometric Euler factors.","opened":true},{"id":"def-complex-exponential","used_for":"Complex powers in Dirichlet series and zeta.","opened":true},{"id":"def-directional-and-weak-sparsity-between-vertex-sets","used_for":"Weak and directional blockade sparsity.","opened":true},{"id":"def-dirichlet-convolution","used_for":"Dirichlet-s